+## 2026-08-05 — Audit rounds 2/3: four "guards" replaced by real fixes (N1, A2, A3, N6) + table unit decoupling (N13/N14)
+
+Local commit `4f9adff` on `flagship-phase2-ct` (parent `4978a4e`; 24 files, +1428/-358).
+**NOT PUSHED** — no GitHub credential on this box (`gh auth status`: not logged in).
+Full finding register: `/beegfs/u/bbg6470/AUDIT_ROUND2_2026-08-05.md` (§9 N1, §10 A2/A3,
+§11 v7 closure, §12 the table-repoint action list that is still UNTAKEN).
+
+Round 1 (commit `4d0b2c0`) and rounds 2/3 (`9f406ce`) had closed several findings by adding a
+*guard* — an abort, or a comment arguing the current configuration is safe. A guard is not a fix:
+it makes the wrong answer loud instead of making the right answer available. These four are now
+actually fixed.
+
+**N1 — 2D CT never evolved B_z.** `src/hydro/ct/ct.cpp`. E1/E2 were assembled only for `ndim > 2`
+and every F3 update sat behind `if (three_d)`, so `dB_z/dt = -curl(E)|_z` was dropped and
+`CT_ProjectBfToCC` copied the frozen face value onto `cons(IB3)`. Fixed with a single integer
+offset `km = (ndim > 2) ? -1 : 0`, which collapses the 4-point k-averages to 2-point in-plane
+averages and makes every d/dz difference identically zero — the 3D expressions are unchanged
+token for token. This matters because in 2D Parthenon returns `ks == ke == 0`
+(`mesh/domain.hpp:216,252`), so `k-1` is out of bounds, not merely degenerate.
+Applied to **every** EMF producer, not just the ideal one: un-gating the ideal path alone would
+advance B_z while silently dropping its Ohmic/ambipolar/Hall diffusion — worse than the freeze,
+because it would look like it was working. `CT_AssembleEMF_GS05` gained an explicit `ndim == 2`
+branch, `E1 = -F_y(B_z)`, `E2 = +F_x(B_z)`; the derivation in the source comment shows this is the
+*exact* z-invariant limit of the 3D upwind formula (the x3-face EMF has identical L/R states, so
+`de_l3 = de_r3 = 0` and the rest telescopes), not an approximation. The x3 flux does not exist in
+2D — the Riemann solve skips it and `ResetFluxes` returns early (`hydro_driver.cpp:115`).
+The abort in `hydro.cpp` is now a one-shot informational report.
+
+**A2 — swindle/multipole reductions were per-partition.** `src/self_gravity/self_gravity.cpp`.
+Now accumulated over the rank's whole block list, once per FillDerived sweep, under a mutex-held
+tick counter. Keyed on `md->StageName()`, not `"base"`: reducing over `"base"` during an RKL2
+sub-stage would use the wrong density. The two `MPI_Allreduce` calls deliberately keep their
+counts at **2 and 10** and are NOT fused into 12 — the reduction algorithm can vary with message
+size, and fusing them would break bit-identity against every existing result.
+
+**A3 — the four sink collectives ran once per partition.** `src/hydro/hydro_driver.cpp`. Now a
+1-region task list over `pmesh->GetBasePartition()`. `CreateSinks` was the worst case: its
+`MPI_MAXLOC` could seed a sink from the densest cell of a *fraction* of the mesh.
+(`DefaultNumPartitions()` is `min(default_num_packs_, block_list.size())` and is therefore not
+rank-uniform; the FillDerived sweep count is.)
+
+**N6** — chemistry counter read-modify-write is mutex-protected.
+
+**N13/N14 — offline tables decoupled from any particular IC.** Both `opacity_table.bin` and
+`eos_table.bin` now carry a stamped header (magic sentinel in the first int64 + version + flags)
+and store data in **cgs**; `Load` applies the *running* simulation's unit system. Legacy headerless
+files still parse (rewind-on-mismatch) and warn. This removes the +0.135 % error on tabulated κ
+and +0.00315 % on the EOS that came from the tables having been generated against a different
+normalization. Regenerated tables verified: `eos_table_hires_v2.bin` is 12,544,112 B (= old + 40
+header bytes), P/cs²/e_sp ratios min = max = 1.000000000000, logT bit-identical, axis origins agree
+to 4.441e-16, and the shift is exactly ρ₀ = 1.366377e-05.
+
